{"i": 153, "kind": "assistant", "session": "dazed-tachometer", "t": 1790532339, "text": "Done — \`dashboard/standalone.html\` is a real app now, no Streamlit involved.\\n\\n**What it is:** a single self-contained HTML file. I exported the actual trained model — all 90 LogisticRegression coefficients, intercepts, and the StandardScaler mean/scale — into a 3.5KB JSON blob embedded in the page. The browser does real inference: scale → logits → softmax. Verified bit-for-bit against sklearn's \`predict_proba\` (max diff 5e-8).\\n\\n**Verified working** (headless Firefox):\\n- All-zero input → Terminal, 42.3% — identical to the Streamlit output\\n- All-2s input → Committed, 52.5%\\n- Batch CSV: dropped a real file, scored 2 samples, Download CSV button rendered\\n- Zero console errors\\n\\n**Features:**\\n- 30-gene input grid + a paste box (drop in 30 comma-separated values to fill all fields at once)\\n- Prediction result card with colored state + per-class probability bars\\n- Batch CSV scoring (drag-drop or browse) with results table + CSV export\\n- Model Evidence section: CV/bootstrap/sample metrics + top SHAP genes (LMNA, PLOD1, C1QBP) — all real numbers from the committed artifacts\\n- Same dark lab theme as the rest of your projects\\n\\n**To use it:** just double-click the file — it has no dependencies and makes no network calls, so \`file://\` works. No venv, no \`streamlit run\`, nothing to install. You can also host it anywhere static (GitHub Pages, etc.) and it just works.\\n\\nThe Streamlit app at \`:8767\` is still running if you want to compare; nothing else changed. If you want it gone, kill it with \`lsof -ti :8767 | xargs kill\`.", "args": {}, "v": 1}
